  "implementation": [
    "Actual PathBuf capacity plus actual boxed Retained<PathBuf> pointee is admitted on the canonical budget before startup storage, loader capture or normalized Save candidate adoption. Existing Save borrows its current witness; candidate/old paths overlap until unchanged atomic Project::write succeeds.",
    "PreparedProject guards actual JSON children plus its actual boxed Retained<Value>, and exactly sizeof<Self> for independent inline handles. Existing accepted/scientific/editor/snapshot/C3 children keep separate original guards. New flags finalize before metadata admission.",
    "Path, metadata and fixed witness identities are checked before the existing atomic accepted-state transaction. Guarded products move to the bridge without clones or post-commit admission. Queued/cancelled/stale products retain coverage through final disposal.",
    "main startup uses the same main-thread Context host as CXX defaults. Runtime options retain an admitted original request, then move it through Loader to the accepted Save path. Parsed raw options and bounded serialization/read/normalization temporaries remain separate finite construction."
  ],
